  "finding_count": 2,
  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "The evaluation completed and passed all of its validity gates / The evaluation still completed and qualified on every validity gate. The sizes in this paper are therefore valid measurements",
      "evidence": "paper_data.json final_evaluation {status completed; outcome qualified; correct true} with no gate fields; grounding_sources final.qualification.status/outcome/correct are the only qualification ids; final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.candidate_diagnostics_trust=unverified; claims_grounding.json claim 16 cites only final.qualification.* and final.metric.final_correct; paper.tex lines 129 and 358",
      "fix": "Restate both places as: the sealed evaluation completed with a qualified outcome (no episode failed and replay matched). Drop the per-gate wording. Replace 'therefore valid measurements' with 'therefore harness-verified upper bounds', keeping the point that the negative outcome concerns only algorithmic improvement.",
      "id": "qualification-gate-overreach-1",
      "issue": "The evaluator record gives only the overall qualification result (status completed, outcome qualified, correct true, final_correct 1.0). It has no gate list and no per-gate diagnostics, so the claim that each validity gate passed cannot be checked. Calling the sizes valid measurements also goes further than the qualification record supports. The record's own trust field marks candidate diagnostics as unverified. The sizes are harness-verified upper bounds, not certified measurements of the minimal perturbation.",
      "section": "Method (Data and protocol) and SI Pre-declared superiority test (app:negative)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Every number in the paper comes from the sealed evaluation record produced by executing the code, and the derivation scripts are included",
      "evidence": "paper.tex line 102 (harness internals described as stated protocol and not checkable), lines 90, 123, 126, 342, 348 and 368 (constants and commits labelled as stated protocol or task data specification); paper_data.json final_evaluation.metrics and episodes contain only verified_k, fractions, comparator ratios, control scores, replay and failure metrics; analysis/derived_stats.json n_rows_derived",
      "fix": "Narrow the sentence to: every measured result (verified sizes, fractions, comparator ratios, control scores, timings) comes from the sealed evaluation record, n is derived from it by the included script, and the protocol constants and data snapshots are reported as stated by the harness and task specification and could not be inspected.",
      "id": "number-provenance-overclaim-1",
      "issue": "This contradicts the paper's own provenance labels. Several visible numbers do not come from the sealed evaluation record. They are attributed elsewhere to the harness's uninspectable stated protocol or to the task's data specification. These include lambda=0.1, tau=1e-6, the 50-comparison player filter, 10 of 20 random subsets, 2,000 bootstrap resamples, the planted-control construction (50 to 80 games, win rates 0.55 to 0.70, enumeration up to size 8), the m<=10tau check, and the dataset commits. The row counts n are derived by the paper's own script from the reported fractions.",
      "section": "SI LLM usage (app:llm)"
    }
  ],
